      "side": 1,
      "message": "Tested the systemd fstab options on an enrolled MAAS compute host:\n- After daemon-reload,verified that the mount was required before nova-compute.\n- On a normal reboot, Vaultlocker unlocked the device, the mount appeared, and Nova started once, after the mount.\n- With Vaultlocker delayed by about 45 seconds, Nova waited and started cleanly.\n- With the mapper unavailable, the host booted, Nova stayed stopped, and the bare instances directory remained empty. Recovery required starting the mount and Nova manually.\nThe reboot experiment used a 180-second device timeout, the committed code uses 600 seconds.",
      "revId": "281890593de318b212e0bf1e9a5382622dc18419",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
